### Day 9 - Authentication Test Evidence

### 1. Health endpoint is public -> expect 200
GET http://localhost:8081/api/health

### 2. Ticket endpoint without token -> expect 401
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets

### 3. Register user -> expect 201 with token
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "testuser09@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 4. Login user -> expect 200 with token
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser09@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 5. Ticket endpoint with USER token -> expect 200
# Replace TOKEN with the token from request 4
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### 6. Create ticket with USER token -> expect 403
# Replace TOKEN with the token from request 4
POST http://localhost:8081/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer not working",
  "description": "Office printer on 3rd floor is jammed.",
  "category": "Hardware",
  "priority": "LOW",
  "createdBy": "testuser09@example.com"
}

### 7. Login admin -> expect 200 with token
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@12345"
}

### 8. Create ticket with ADMIN token -> expect 201
# Replace TOKEN with the token from request 7
POST http://localhost:8081/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer not working",
  "description": "Office printer on 3rd floor is jammed.",
  "category": "Hardware",
  "priority": "LOW",
  "createdBy": "testuser09@example.com"
}
